    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13110" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dentāle</span></b> , is, and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dentālia</span></b> ,
		ium (only the <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>plural</i> class.; sing.
			post-class.), n.
			dens, <i>no.</i> I. B., <i>the share-beam</i>, to which the vomer or ploughshare was
			attached. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.,
				plur., <i><span class="en">Verg. G. 1, 172</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 2, 2,
				24</span></i>.—<i>Sing.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">genus vomerum toto porrectum dentali,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					18, 18, 48, § 171</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Meton.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sulco terens dentalia,</span>”
				<i>a ploughshare</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Pers.
					1, 73</span></i>
			.</div>
